## Block

- No production file changed. No implementation commit exists.
- Block 1: `apps/storytime/__tests__/phase3-phoneme-bank.test.ts` line 46 reads
  `week.focus.element.graphemes` for every shipped week. The shipped `w08.json` is a review week
  (`meta.kind: "review"`) with no `focus.element`, so the test throws `TypeError` before it checks
  the bank. No app change can add an element to a review week.
  - One-line fix: `const taught = new Set(weeks.flatMap((week) => week.focus.element?.graphemes ?? []));`.
- Block 2: `apps/storytime/__tests__/phase3-decodable-ui.test.tsx` line 136 searches a page with
  `entry.text?.toLowerCase().includes(word)`. The F28 fix makes the capital word `Nan` of `w02`
  the first blend word, so `word` is `"Nan"`. A lower-case page text never includes `"Nan"`, and the
  test fails before it capitalizes the page word.
  - One-line fix: `...includes(word.toLowerCase())`.
  - This fix also lets `blendPlanForWord` treat a capital word like its lower-case form, as F28
    requires. A workaround in the UI would hide the pure-function defect.
- Report: `measure/runs/storytime_app_rebuild_20261025/green-a23c435.log`.

